  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f$ be differentiable for all $x$. If $f(1)=-2$ and $f^{\\prime}(x) \\geq 2$ for $x \\in[1,6]$, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gVgRh",
      "text": "\n$f(6) \\geq 8$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ax8iE",
      "text": "\n$f(6) < 8$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9wMYh",
      "text": "\n$f(6) < 5$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "y1A9r",
      "text": "\n$f(6)=5$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As $f(1)=-2 \\quad \\& f^{\\prime}(x) \\geq 2 \\quad \\forall x \\in[1,6]$\nApplying Lagrange's mean value theorem\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{f(6)-f(1)}{5}=f^{\\prime}(c) \\geq 2 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow f(6) \\geq 10+f(1) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow f(6) \\geq 10-2 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow f(6) \\geq 8 .\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
